body:
@pedroigor Thanks, with `TenantResolver`, `OAuth2Auth` have already been precalculated in the recorder per each tenant configuration available in the `application.properties`, and since the only thing that `TenantResolver` does is getting a tenant id out of `RoutingContext`, I'd say it is safe enough to relax around `TenantResolver` and only block if `TenantConfigResolver` is used.
What do you think ?
(We can also consider tweaking `TenantConfigResolver` now before it has been documented ?)

@pedroigor Sure, see what you mean. I suppose it is more likely to happen with `TenantConfigResolver` which would load the config from DB...If we ever have a case of `TenantResolver` attempting to do something costly then we can always say that in this case you have to use `TenantConfigResolver`. We can even update `TenantResolver` javadocs now and say that `this provider must be non-blocking and only use RoutingContext to get the tenant id, TenantConfigResolver should be used if the tenant or configuration resolution is blocking`, something like that (unless TenantConfigResolver is made unblocking too)

> Could you elaborate more about tweaking TenantConfigResolver ?

Have it return `CompletableFuture<OidcTenantConfig>` ?
